    "clos": [
      {
        "No.": "1",
        "CLO Name": "CLO1",
        "CLO Details": "Describe basic properties and find the limit of a function\nLO1.1 Find the domain, range, zeros and analyze the symmetry of the graph; create new functions from old functions.\nLO1.2 Find the slope and write an equation of a line; describe how a function changes under graph translations.\nLO1.3 Compute the limit of a function using graphs and limit laws, including the Squeeze's Theorem.\nLO1.4 Find limits at infinity and infinity limits, and apply in finding asymptotes of a function.\nLO1.5 Identify where a function is continuous; use the Intermedia Value Theorem to show that an equation has a solution."
      },
      {
        "No.": "2",
        "CLO Name": "CLO2",
        "CLO Details": "Calculate derivatives of a function\nLO2.1 Find the average rate of change; identify derivative as the limit of a difference quotient.\nLO2.2 Recognize derivative as the instantaneous velocity and the slope of tangent lines.\nLO2.3 Find derivatives using basic formulas and the sum, difference, product, quotient, chain rules."
      },
      {
        "No.": "3",
        "CLO Name": "CLO3",
        "CLO Details": "Use derivatives to analyze a function and to solve applications\nLO3.1 Use implicit differentiation to find derivatives and to solve related rates problems.\nLO3.2 Find linear approximation of a function; calculate differentials and apply in calculating errors of approximation.\nLO3.3 Apply Rolle's Theorem and Mean Value Theorem to a function; find critical numbers and absolute extrema of a function.\nLO3.4 Identify local extrema, and describe the monotonicity of a function; solve optimization problems.\nLO3.5 Recognize acceleration as second derivative; determine inflection points and describe the concavity of a function.\nLO3.6 Use Newton method to approximate solutions of an equation."
      },
      {
        "No.": "4",
        "CLO Name": "CLO4",
        "CLO Details": "Calculate integrals and find area under the graph of a function\nLO4.1 Use Riemann sums to approximate area; recognize area as a definite integral which is the limit of Riemann sums.\nLO4.2 Apply the Fundamental Theorems of Calculus to find derivatives of integrals, and to evaluate definite integrals.\nLO4.3 Recognize indefinite integrals as anti-derivatives; find integrals using basic formulas and the techniques of substitution and integration by parts.\nLO4.4 Use integration to solve applications and to compute the average value of a function.\nLO4.5 Approximate definite integrals using Midpoint, Trapezoidal and Simpson rules.\nLO4.6 Determine if an improper integral converges."
      },
      {
        "No.": "5",
        "CLO Name": "CLO5",
        "CLO Details": "Solve a system of linear equations using Gaussian elimination\nLO5.1 Identify if a matrix is in echelon forms; carry a matrix into an echelon using row operations; calculate the rank of a matrix.\nLO5.2 Use echelon matrices to solve/describe the solution set of a linear system."
      },
      {
        "No.": "6",
        "CLO Name": "CLO6",
        "CLO Details": "Perform basic operations on matrices and manipulate matrix transformations\nLO6.1 Perform addition, scalar multiplication and transpose of matrices; verify if a matrix is symmetric.\nLO6.2 Multiply two matrices of appropriate sizes; transform between a linear system and a matrix equation.\nLO6.3 Determine the matrix of a linear transformation; use properties of linear transformations in solving problems."
      },
      {
        "No.": "7",
        "CLO Name": "CLO7",
        "CLO Details": "Find the determinant, inverse and diagonalization of a matrix\nLO7.1 Compute the cofactors and the determinant of a matrix; analyze determinants in relation with row/column operations.\nLO7.2 Check if a matrix is invertible; find the adjugate and the inverse of a matrix; use properties of inverses and determinants in solving problems.\nLO7.3 Solve a system of linear equations using inverse matrices or Cramer's rule.\nLO7.4 Find the characteristic polynomial, eigenvalues and eigenvectors to diagonalize a matrix; check if a matrix is diagonalizable."
      },
      {
        "No.": "8",
        "CLO Name": "CLO8",
        "CLO Details": "Manipulate vector operations and linear transformations in R^3.\nLO8.1 Manipulate vector operations; find equations of lines.\nLO8.2 Compute the dot product and the angle between two vectors; find the projection of a vector on another vector and manipulate equations of planes.\nLO8.3 Compute the cross product; analyze areas and volumns in relation with dot and cross products.\nLO8.4 Determine linear transformations in R^3 and discuss applications in computer graphic."
      },
      {
        "No.": "9",
        "CLO Name": "CLO9",
        "CLO Details": "Find the dimension and bases of a subspace\nLO9.1 Determine if a subset of vectors is a subspace; describe the subspace spanned by a set of vectors.\nLO9.2 Check if a set of vectors are independent; determine if a set of vectors form a basis.\nLO9.3 Find a basis and the dimension of a subspace; analyze the rank in relation with the dimension of the column, row and the null space of a matrix.\nLO9.4 Compute dot product and length of vectors; check if a set of vectors are orthogonal or orthonormal; write a vector as a linear combination of an orthogonal basis."
      }
    ],
